==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=riddle (disambiguation)|mul=Riddle}}

===Etymology 1===
{{etyl|enm}} ''[[redel]]'', ''[[redels]]'' from {{etyl|ang}} ''[[rædels|rǣdels]]'', ''[[rædelse|rǣdelse]]'' "counsel, opinion, imagination, riddle" from {{proto|Germanic|rǣdislijan|counsel, conjecture|lang=}}. Akin to {{etyl|osx|-}} ''[[radisli|rādisli]]'' ({{etyl|nld|-}} ''[[raadsel]]''), {{etyl|goh|-}} ''[[radisle|rādisle]]'' ({{etyl|deu|-}} ''[[Rätsel]]'' "riddle"), {{etyl|ang|-}} ''[[rædan|rǣdan]]'' "to read, advise, interpret"

===Pronunciation===
*: {{rhymes|ɪdəl}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[verbal]] [[puzzle]], [[mystery]], or other [[problem]] of an [[intellectual]] nature, such as "It's black, and white, and red all over. What is it?"
# A [[sieve]].

=====Synonyms=====
* [[enigma]]
* [[conundrum]]
* [[brain-teaser]]

=====Derived terms=====
* [[riddler]]
* [[riddle stick]]
* [[a riddle wrapped up in an enigma]]

