===Etymology 2===
{{etyl|enm}} ''[[ridelen]]'' "to sift" from ''[[riddil]]'', ''[[ridelle]]'' "sieve" from {{etyl|ang}} ''[[hriddel]]'' "sieve", alteration of earlier ''[[hridder]]'', ''[[hrider|hrīder]]'' from {{proto|Germanic|hridan|sieve|lang=}} from {{proto|Germanic|hrid-|to shake|lang=}} from {{proto|Indo-European|krei||lang=}}. Akin to {{etyl|deu|-}} ''[[Reiter]]'' "sieve", {{etyl|non|-}} ''[[hreinn]]'' "pure, clean", {{etyl|goh|-}} ''[[hreini]]'' "pure, clean", {{etyl|got|-}} ''[[hrains]]'' "clean, pure". More at [[rinse]]

====Verb====
{{en-verb|riddles|riddling|riddled}}

# to fill with [[hole]]s
#: ''The shots from his gun began to '''riddle''' the target.''
# to fill or spread throughout; to [[pervade]]
#: ''Your argument is '''riddled''' with errors.''
# to [[solve]], [[answer]], or [[explicate]] a riddle or question
#: '''''Riddle''' me this....'', meaning ''Answer the following question.''
# to put something through a [[sieve]]
#: ''You have to '''riddle''' the gravel before you lay it on the road.''

